  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="26a64855-31b2-563c-8903-3a4ecc6d371a" activityNameId="7cb5a99e-37e5-5417-833e-8bbfcb3bef60" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Nuclear power plant, boiling water reactor 1000MW</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Nuclear power plant, boiling water reactor 1000MW
The module is based on "nuclear power plant, boiling water reactor 1000MW", CH. Only two differences are: the supply mix of electricity, US instead of CH;
UUID: f8860edc-546d-3cef-90a5-2b2ee194af1b
The module includes materials, energy and transport requirements used for construction of the plant. Land-use is included with the assumption of 40 years operation. Disposal of non-contaminated material from dismantling is also included, whereas contaminated materials are attributed to the operation.
Location: Swiss data on one specific plant adapted to USA.
Technology: The described plant Leibstadt (CH) started commercial operation at the end of 1984. It belongs to the 1000 MW class (net installed capacity has been upgraded in steps from the original 990 MW to 1165 MW at the end of 1999). It has a GE (USA) designed primary circuit, a Mark III containment, and a cooling tower. This module can be assumed to be representative for the boiling water reactors of the same class in USA.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f8860edc-546d-3cef-90a5-2b2ee194af1b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="9aaa4753-f7ef-5e0d-bcb0-bc5f01164c5b" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">US</shortname>
        <comment>
